cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "DPT Toolkit: An Open-Source Toolkit for Discovery Plane Theory"

message: >
  If you use this software in academic research, please cite both the
  DPT Toolkit and the associated Discovery Plane Theory publications.

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Akhtar
    given-names: Mohammad Amir Khusru

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-08-02"

license: Apache-2.0

repository-code: "https://github.com/USERNAME/DPT-Toolkit"

abstract: >
  DPT Toolkit is an open-source implementation of Discovery Plane Theory (DPT),
  providing a complete workflow for transparent and reproducible evaluation of
  scientific research questions, including Discovery Complexity (DC), Question
  Compression (QC), Discovery Frontier extraction, dominance analysis, budget
  constraints, utility optimisation, sensitivity analysis, dynamic coordinates,
  reliability assessment, and visualisation.

keywords:
  - Discovery Plane Theory
  - Discovery Complexity
  - Question Compression
  - Research Question Evaluation
  - Research Methodology
  - Scientific Discovery
  - Decision Science
  - Research Screening
  - Research Planning
  - Open Science

references:

  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: Akhtar
        given-names: Mohammad Amir Khusru
    title: "The Mystery of Questions: Why Some Questions Change the World"
    year: 2026
    publisher: Amazon
    url: "https://a.co/d/09f5Hi4W"

  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Akhtar
        given-names: Mohammad Amir Khusru
    title: "Discovery Plane Theory: A Formal and Reproducible Framework for Scientific Question Formation, Discovery Complexity, and Question Compression"
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21725071"

  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Akhtar
        given-names: Mohammad Amir Khusru
    title: "Evaluating AI-Generated Scientific Questions with Discovery Plane Theory: A Repeated-Measures Computational Benchmark Across Twenty Scientific Fields (Version V1)"
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21738143"
